          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            There are many different notions of real numbers in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Archimedean+ordered+field"} Archimedean ordered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+extension"} field extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            of the field of (sequential, modulated)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} R
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{R}_C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphisms"} ring homomorphisms
            of ordered fields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi C
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi R
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_C \hookrightarrow R \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}_D
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_D
            is the ordered field of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
            \- the homomorphism into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_D
            always exists since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_D
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
            Archimedean ordered field. In general the ring homomorphisms are not provably
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            unless the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
            coincide. Thus, there are many different notions of the analytic limited principle of omniscience; the analytic limited principles of omniscience are defined for each Archimedean ordered field extension of the Cauchy real numbers.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Archimedean+ordered+field"} Archimedean ordered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+extension"} field extension
              of the field of (sequential, modulated)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} R
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{R}_C
              %strong analytic LPO
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              states that the usual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+relation"} apartness relation
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+relation"} decidable
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \neq y
              or
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trichotomy"} trichotomy
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
